 "rule": {
  "rule_id": "woody_role_to_frequency_class_v1",
  "text": "Each (taxon, place family) pair gets one habitat role read from the cited source wording; the class follows only from the role: edificator (source: dominates / forms stands / 'главным образом', 'чистые', 'сплошные заросли') -> ubiquitous 8; component (source names the habitat as a typical place of growth / undergrowth / 'повсеместно') -> common 4; occasional (source: 'встречается', admixture, secondary habitat, habitat named once among several, or source says the genus occupies 'less space') -> contextual 2; rare (source: 'only in southern districts', 'дефицитный', unconfirmed native status, or habitat implied only indirectly) -> rare 1. Presence does not change by season (woody plants persist all year); seasonal state is derived separately from phenology.",
  "classes": {
   "edificator": [
    "ubiquitous",
    8
   ],
   "component": [
    "common",
    4
   ],
   "occasional": [
    "contextual",
    2
   ],
   "rare": [
    "rare",
    1
   ]
  },
  "overlay_rule": "pf_forest_track and pf_hunting_ground are overlays on woodland: each taxon takes its max class over pf_conifer_woodland, pf_mixed_woodland, pf_broadleaf_woodland (forest_track) and additionally pf_forest_edge and pf_bog (hunting_ground), capped at 'component' (a taxon confined to one source place family cannot become guaranteed-present/edificator on the overlay pf just by dominating that one habitat). Derived by scripts/build.mjs; an explicit authored row for the overlay pf is allowed and wins over the capped overlay when its own class is higher. Fixed 2026-09-26 per verifier note (VERIFICATION.md#tree_habitat_presence.csv item 1): previously uncapped, lipa/leshina got guaranteed presence on every pf_forest_track and bagulnik on every pf_hunting_ground.",
  "region": "region_novgorod_land (southern-taiga Novgorod land). Taxa are universal categories; region permission is expressed only by these presence rows.",
  "not_measured": "Classes are an editorial reading of qualitative sources, not biological abundance or encounter probability. Colchin 1968 table I counts are artefact counts and are NOT used to set classes."
 },
